# Google Calendar integration (read-only)
#
# This app connects to Google Calendar entirely from the browser using Google's
# "token client" flow (Google Identity Services) — there is no backend, no
# authorization redirect, and no client secret involved. Only a public Client ID
# is needed, which is safe to expose in frontend code.
#
# Setup:
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or select) a project.
# 2. APIs & Services > Library > enable the "Google Calendar API".
# 3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen > add the scope
#      https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
#    and add your own Google account as a test user if the app is left in
#    "Testing" publishing status.
# 4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID.
#      - Application type: Web application
#      - Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173
#        (add your deployed URL here too, later)
#      - No redirect URI is required.
# 5. Copy the generated Client ID (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com) below.
#
# Never put a client SECRET in this file or anywhere in this repo — this
# integration doesn't use one, and doesn't need one.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
